<urn:atm:triage:finding/AM6-BENCHMARK-BASELINE-FALSE-CLAIM-UNCORRECTED>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AM6-BENCHMARK-BASELINE-FALSE-CLAIM-UNCORRECTED" ;
  triage:title "AL9-benchmark-gate.md's false baseline row is not corrected, and am6-closure-proof.md substitutes a new run instead of a real comparison" ;
  triage:description "quality-mgr QA-AM6-1 (BLOCKING-2, req-qa + arch-qa, independently confirmed via git-log analysis): docs/plans/phase-al/AL9-benchmark-gate.md's frozen UDS-f1 baseline table cites site/reports/send-message-benchmark/20260801-072313.590684-mac-arm64-01-uds-f1.json with source_revision 3ec7ce1f and p50=14,715.31/s, but that artifact has held its actual content (source_revision fb6b26363c5b, passed=false, 25/1000 messages accepted, 'sqlite connection budget exceeded') since its first commit on 2026-08-01 -- it has never been a passing run. The false table row was added later, on 2026-08-07. This pre-existing defect is not introduced by this PR, but AM.6's own deliverable is to 're-run the full AL.9 proof suite and compare final benchmark with its raw baseline/result artifact' -- am6-closure-proof.md correctly identifies the artifact as failed and supplies a new, independently-verified-legitimate M5 passing run (354,000/354,000, p50=17,779.88) instead, but a new isolated passing run is not the same as the required baseline comparison, and the doc never corrects AL9-benchmark-gate.md's own false claim. Fix requires: (a) correct or retract AL9-benchmark-gate.md's false table row for this artifact, (b) either locate a genuinely valid pre-AL baseline artifact and perform the real comparison the deliverable requires, or explicitly document why no valid pre-AL baseline exists and what standard of proof the new M5 result satisfies in its place." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-am" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "doc-accuracy" ;
  triage:severity "blocking" ;
